## Status: complete

## Item 1: F7, scripts/review-cards.py (commit 2f8ee4a6)

- The fault: the card cut the lower half of out/<name>/render.png as the views. That crop is only
  right when the sheet holds a reference row on top.
- The finding: src/render/page.ts draws the reference row only when the request carries a
  referenceUrl, and src/cli/forge.ts (line 322) sends it only when the asset declares
  `reference`. A sheet without one holds the views only.
- The fix: the script reads out/<name>/views/*.png, computes the height of the view rows
  (GAP = 4, cols = min(4, count)) and compares it with the sheet height. With no reference row,
  the whole sheet becomes the views and a dark panel with the text "no mockup" fills the mockup
  slot. With a reference, the old crop stays.
- The check: out/prop-cards/duck.png shows the whole duck with its head, and
  out/prop-cards/paint-pot.png shows the paint in the pot. The card for towel-stack-a, which has
  a reference, is byte-identical to the card before the fix.
- Weak: none known.

## Item 2: the duck fixes (commit f098d5b9)

- F1, the wings stood 34 mm out and read as arms. The wing options changed: wingTurn 68 -> 95,
  wingScale 0.62 -> 0.26, wingOut 0.03 -> 0.05, wingRest -45 kept. The wing now lies flat on the
  body's side with its tip toward the tail.
- The measuring tool: measure/runs/asset_chibi_sprouts_r1_20261022/wing-probe.ts rebuilds the
  kind's trunk, raycasts its real smooth-union surface, and reports the worst protrusion for
  each set of options. The worst protrusion is 5.8 mm; the limit is 8 mm.
- F2, the catch-light was doubled and too large. The kind's painted glint is off (glint: 0) and
  the white sphere radius is 0.0025 m (was 0.004 m). One glint shows on each eye.
- The dot sits on the merged body's surface: the kind's smooth union pulls the surface in from the
  skull by up to 5.5 mm, so the ray hits sdf.smoothUnion(0.05, b.trunk, b.skull).
- The check: the mech-check line is
  {"asset":"duck","ok":true,"forgeAll":{"exitCode":0,"warnings":[]},"triangles":6550,"bottomY":0,
  "files":{"glb":true,"stats":true,"render":true,"sprites":true,"glbBytes":1164936},
  "typecheckExit":0,"failures":[]}. cutout-check prints "result ok". The card is
  out/prop-cards/duck.png.
- Weak: the wings are subtle. `forge inspect duck` reports coverts at 0.9% of the silhouette in
  the side view and flight as barely visible. The wing reads as a fold, not as an arm.
- The duck brief holds the F1 and F2 record in its Known differences.

